-- title:
--   Residue pairing Theta: kernel and residue formula
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$, an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$, and $N\neq 0$, and write $F=K(\bar\jmath,\bar\jmath_N)$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` of `LaurentSeries K` generated by `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`. Assume $F$ is a curve over $K$ (principal divisors of degree $0$, finite residue extensions, $\Omega[F/K]$ free of rank one over $F$), that every nonzero Kähler differential has a divisor of its local differential orders, that the uniformiser differential $\mathrm{d}t_v$ spans $\Omega[F/K]$ at every place, that $\Omega[F/K]$ is nontrivial, and `hagree`: for every $\omega\neq 0$ the Weil functional `weilOfKaehler` is nonzero, lies in $\Omega(K_\omega)$ for $K_\omega=$`canonicalDivisorOf`$\,\omega$, and $\Omega(D)\ni$ `weilOfKaehler` forces $D\le K_\omega$. Assume further $N\neq 0$ in $K$, $m\ge 1$, that the finset $SS$ has as members exactly the supersingular places (rational affine geometric places whose $\bar\jmath$-value lies in `ssJSet p K`), and that the divisor $D'$ equals `weightDivisor K N m` minus $1$ at each supersingular place whose `placeWidth` divides $m$, and equals `weightDivisor K N m` at every other place. Then there is a $K$-linear map $\Theta$ from `SSCarrier p N K hp5 (2m)`, the $K$-valued functions on the places that are supersingular with `placeWidth` dividing $m$, to the $K$-dual of $\Omega(D')$ (the annihilator of `adeleBddPrincipal` $D'$ inside the dual of the adele space) such that: (i) $\Theta v=0$ holds precisely when $v=$`resFnFun p N K hp5 m G` for some $G$ in the Riemann–Roch space of `weightDivisor K N m`, i.e. $v$ is the tuple of leading coefficients $\mathrm{ev}_x(t_x^{\,\mathrm{poleOrder}}G)$ of such a $G$; and (ii) for every $v$ and every $\omega\neq 0$ in $\Omega[F/K]$ whose Weil functional lies in $\Omega(D')$, the value of $\Theta v$ at that functional equals $\sum_{x\in SS}$`kaehlerResidueTerm` $\omega$ of the constant family with value `liftFun p N K hp5 (2m) v` at $x$, that is the sum over supersingular $x$ of $\mathrm{Tr}_{\kappa(x)/K}\,\mathrm{res}_x(\tilde v\cdot c_x(\omega))$, where $\tilde v$ is the chosen lift of $v$.
--
--   This is the connecting map of the sequence relating $L(D_{2m})$, the supersingular leading-coefficient space and $H^1(D')$, transported through Serre duality and written out by local residues: its kernel is the image of the restriction map on Riemann–Roch sections, and its values against Weil differentials coming from Kähler differentials are sums of residues over the supersingular places. It supplies the pairing used in [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window).
